0.7.9:
[x] - The click-to-select tool keeps working after the app preview reloads, instead of going dead until you click it twice.
[x] - DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (Fireworks) is a new choice in the model dropdown — 1M context, reads images, and faster/cheaper than V4 Pro. Checked Muse Spark 1.3 the same day: still registered but our Meta account cannot reach it (404), so it stays greyed out.
[x] - On a ChatGPT/Codex-authenticated thread, Leo no longer shows you raw JSON before it asks its question.
[x] - You can rate a reply with 👍/👎 while Leo is still writing it, instead of waiting for the run to finish.
[x] - The pointer/select-element tool in the purple feedback bubble now works on phones and tablets: tap to highlight, tap Use this to confirm, and a banner with a Cancel button means you are never stuck in selection mode with no way out.
[x] - The screenshot annotator's arrow, box and text tools no longer refuse to draw on top of an annotation you already made — and drawing near an existing arrow no longer drags it across the image. A new Move tool repositions annotations when you actually want that.
[x] - Leo knows about the recipes you saved to your personal cookbook, so you can say "use the design system I saved from my other Leo" instead of picking it from the /cookbook menu every time.
[x] - The "2 JavaScript errors detected" notice still appears in a custom Leo mode, but it no longer ships the errors to that agent on its own — the Show Leo box starts unchecked there and stays checked in Beginner/Engineer/Ticket mode. A custom mode is somebody else's agent and may have no idea what to do with a stack trace; tick the box yourself when it does.
